---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Statement from '../components/Statement.astro';
import { business } from '../data/business';

const title = 'About — Noven';
const description =
  'Noven is a small UK business that helps service firms get found when their customers ask AI assistants who to use. Plain pricing, no guarantees we can’t keep, no invented results.';
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <section class="hero hero--rules">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>What is Noven?</h1>
      <p class="lede" data-reveal>
        A small business with one job: making sure that when your customers ask an AI assistant to
        recommend someone who does what you do, your name is in the answer.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap split split--sticky">
      <div data-reveal>
        <h2>Why does Noven exist?</h2>
      </div>
      <div data-reveal>
        <p>
          Because a real shift is happening quietly. A meaningful share of people now ask ChatGPT,
          Google, Copilot or Perplexity for recommendations they would previously have researched
          themselves — and the businesses being recommended mostly have no idea why, while the
          businesses being left out have no idea it's happening.
        </p>
        <p>
          Most of what determines who gets recommended is unglamorous and fixable: whether the AI
          systems can read your website, whether the facts about your business agree with each other
          across the web, and whether anything you've published actually answers the questions
          customers ask. Almost no small firm has had this looked at. Noven exists to do exactly
          that, at prices a small firm can justify.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--tint">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="split" style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
        <div data-reveal>
          <h2>How do we work?</h2>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="stages">
          <div class="stage" data-reveal>
            <div class="stage-head">
              <h3>Plainly</h3>
            </div>
            <div class="stage-body">
              <p>
                We write reports in ordinary English, we price in round numbers, and we tell you
                when you don't need us. Our audit exists partly so we can say "you're fine" and mean
                it.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="stage" data-reveal>
            <div class="stage-head">
              <h3>Honestly about uncertainty</h3>
            </div>
            <div class="stage-body">
              <p>
                Nobody controls what an AI assistant says. We work on the inputs these systems
                demonstrably rely on and we measure the results, but we don't guarantee outcomes,
                and we don't show numbers that can't be checked.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="stage" data-reveal>
            <div class="stage-head">
              <h3>In the open</h3>
            </div>
            <div class="stage-body">
              <p>
                This website is built with the same methods we sell. Everything on it is readable by
                the AI crawlers, the facts are stated in machine-readable form, and the FAQ answers
                real questions. If the approach works, you'll be able to see it working on us.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--invert">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div data-reveal>
        <h2>Who's behind it?</h2>
        {
          business.founderPhoto && (
            <figure class="founder-photo">
              <img src={business.founderPhoto} alt={business.founder} width="600" height="750" />
            </figure>
          )
        }
      </div>
      <div>
        <div data-reveal>
          <p>
            Noven is run by {business.founder}, from {business.basedIn}. One person does the work —
            when you email Noven, you're emailing him, and the report you get back is one he wrote.
          </p>
          <p>
            Kieran spent nearly ten years in operations at {business.founderFormerEmployer}, making
            sure containers were sent and arrived as planned. That work is mostly about keeping
            information accurate and consistent across systems that don't naturally agree, which is
            a large part of what this work is too. He came across this problem by chance while
            building a few websites, and found it interesting enough to build a business around.
            {
              business.founderLinkedIn && (
                <>
                  {' '}The full work history is on <a href={business.founderLinkedIn}>LinkedIn</a>.
                </>
              )
            }
          </p>
          {
            !business.founderLinkedIn && (
              <p class="flag">
                [PLACEHOLDER: LinkedIn profile URL — set `founderLinkedIn` in
                src/data/business.ts. It links here and joins the structured data as `sameAs`.]
              </p>
            )
          }
          {
            !business.founderPhoto && (
              <p class="flag">
                [PLACEHOLDER: founder photograph — add the file to site/public and set
                `founderPhoto` in src/data/business.ts.]
              </p>
            )
          }
          <p>
            Noven works with clients across the {business.areaServedLabel}, and the work is done
            remotely — there's nothing about it that needs us in the same room.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <Statement cite="One person, one service, and a written record of everything promised.">
        Small enough that you always know <em>who did the work.</em>
      </Statement>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
